{
    "background_story": "Muffin, a curious cat, lived with her owner, a renowned economist. As she spent more time watching her owner work, Muffin became fascinated with the concept of microeconomics. She began to notice how the household's resources were allocated, observing how her owner made decisions about what to buy and when. Muffin even started her own little 'business', trading catnip and treats with the neighbor's cat. She quickly learned about supply and demand, adjusting her prices according to the market. As her owner worked on a paper about consumer behavior, Muffin would sit by her side, 'helping' by batting at the keyboard. Together, they explored the intricacies of microeconomic theory, with Muffin providing a unique feline perspective. Her owner often joked that Muffin was the purr-fect example of a rational consumer.",
